  "notes": "USAGE:\nExtremely common as a suffix-like element attached to nouns: X{志向|しこう} means \"X-oriented\" or \"tendency toward X.\" This pattern is productive and can be applied to many nouns.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {健康|けんこう}{志向|しこう}: health-consciousness\n- {安定|あんてい}{志向|しこう}: stability-oriented, preference for stability\n- {上昇|じょうしょう}{志向|しこう}: upward aspiration\n- {自然|しぜん}{志向|しこう}: nature-oriented\n- ブランド{志向|しこう}: brand-conscious\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\nDistinguish from {嗜好|しこう} (preference, taste — especially for food, drink, tobacco), {思考|しこう} (thinking, thought process), and {施行|しこう} (enforcement of a law). All are read しこう but have different meanings and kanji.",
